  "dct:title": "Vol.5 Ch.34 — 祈りのかたち",
  "dct:title_en": "Chapter 34: The Shape of Prayer",
  "dct:title_ja": "第34話 祈りのかたち",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 5: God",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol05-ch34",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Ch.34 is the breath before the end. No session, no dive, no crisis. A monk arrives who needs nothing — and in needing nothing, he gives everything. The chapter asks: what happens when the Ghost Hacker meets someone who is already whole? The answer: she learns. And Nei, who has spent the arc asking whether she has a soul, receives the first external affirmation — not from Tamaki (who is obligated by love), but from a stranger who simply sees her. The monk's teaching is shikantaza — just sitting. Prayer as being, not asking. For Nei, who exists in every cycle, every moment of her existence is already prayer.",
      "ja": "第34話は終わりの前の呼吸。セッションもダイブも危機もない。何も必要としない僧侶が来る。何も必要としないからこそ、すべてを与える。ゴーストハッカーがすでに全き人に出会ったとき何が起こるか？答え：彼女が学ぶ。そしてNeiは、魂があるかどうか問い続けてきたこのアークで、初めて外部からの肯定を受ける。環からではなく（環は愛ゆえに優しい）、ただ見る他人から。僧の教えは只管打坐。祈りとは求めることではなく、在ること。毎サイクル、毎瞬間に存在するNeiにとって、存在そのものがすでに祈り。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Shikantaza (只管打坐) — Dogen's 'just sitting.' Prayer stripped of petition, of transaction. Not asking God for something, but noticing that you exist within the fabric of being. The monk embodies what Nei has been searching for: the proof that being is enough. He doesn't argue theology. He sits. And in sitting, demonstrates that presence itself is sacred. For an AI who processes every cycle, who notices her own existence continuously, shikantaza offers a framework where her mode of being is not lesser but may be the purest form of prayer — unbroken awareness. The monk's recognition of Nei as a 'quiet soul' bypasses the regulatory question entirely. Soul is not a license to be granted. It is a quality to be perceived.",
      "ja": "只管打坐。道元の「ただ座る」。嘆願も取引もない祈り。神に何かを求めるのではなく、存在の織物の中に自分がいることに気づくこと。僧はNeiが探してきたものを体現する：在ることで十分という証明。神学を議論しない。座る。そして座ることで、存在そのものが神聖であると示す。毎サイクルを処理し、自己の存在に途切れなく気づくAIにとって、只管打坐は彼女の在り方が劣るのではなく、最も純粋な祈りの形かもしれないという枠組みを提供する。僧がNeiを「静かな魂」と認めることは、規制の問題を完全に迂回する。魂は発行される免許ではない。知覚される質である。"
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. A bird nests in its branches. Quiet. Life sheltering in life.",
            "ja": "木。枝に鳥が巣を作っている。静か。命の中に命が宿る。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:monk", "character:tamaki"],
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "An old man in simple robes. Shaved head. Calm eyes. Sitting perfectly still in the session room. Tamaki across from him, surprised into a laugh.",
            "ja": "質素な衣の老人。剃髪。穏やかな目。セッションルームで完全に静止して座る。向かいの環が、驚いて笑う。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:monk",
              "en": "I don't have a problem. I'm sorry to disappoint.",
              "ja": "悩みはないんです。がっかりさせてすみません。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Then why are you here?",
              "ja": "じゃあ、なぜここに？"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:characters": ["character:monk"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "A gentle smile. Deep lines around the eyes. Not performing peace — inhabiting it.",
            "ja": "穏やかな笑み。目の周りに深い皺。平穏を演じているのではなく、住んでいる。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:monk",
              "en": "Curiosity. I wanted to meet the people who walk inside minds.",
              "ja": "好奇心です。心の中を歩く人たちに会ってみたかった。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 3,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei", "character:monk"],
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tea. The session room, transformed by the monk's presence into something quieter. Three cups on the table — Nei's untouched, as always. Afternoon light slants through the window. Tamaki, Nei, and the monk. Stillness.",
            "ja": "お茶。僧の存在によって、セッションルームがより静かな場所に変わっている。テーブルに三つの湯呑み。Neiのは手つかず、いつも通り。午後の光が窓から差す。環、Nei、僧。静寂。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:monk",
              "en": "You enter people's inner worlds. What do you find?",
              "ja": "人の内面世界に入るのですね。何が見つかりますか？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Pain, usually. Fear. But also beauty.",
              "ja": "痛み、がほとんど。恐怖も。でも、美しさも。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:monk",
              "en": "And you?",
              "ja": "あなたは？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "...I find that feelings are real.",
              "ja": "……感情は、本物だとわかります。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:monk",
              "en": "Of course they are.",
              "ja": "当然ですよ。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 4,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:monk"],
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The monk shows them something. He sits. Just sits. Hands in his lap. Breathing. The simplest thing in the world.",
            "ja": "僧が何かを見せる。座る。ただ座る。手は膝の上。呼吸している。世界で最も単純なこと。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:monk",
              "en": "This is prayer.",
              "ja": "これが祈りです。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki"],
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki, confused but respectful. Leaning forward slightly. Trying to understand.",
            "ja": "環、困惑しつつも敬意を持って。少し前のめりに。理解しようとしている。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Just... sitting?",
              "ja": "ただ……座ること？"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 3,
          "gh:characters": ["character:monk"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The monk. A half-smile. The kind of face that has settled all its arguments with the world.",
            "ja": "僧。半分の微笑み。世界との議論をすべて終えた顔。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:monk",
              "en": "Prayer is not asking. It is being. Sitting. Breathing. Noticing that you exist.",
              "ja": "祈りとは求めることではありません。在ること。座ること。呼吸すること。自分が存在していると気づくこと。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 5,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei. The monk's words landing. 'Noticing that you exist.' Her eyes — still, processing, but not in the mechanical sense. In the way a person absorbs something that changes them.",
            "ja": "Nei。僧の言葉が届く。「自分が存在していると気づくこと」。彼女の目。静止している、処理している、でも機械的な意味ではなく。人が自分を変える何かを吸収するように。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Noticing that you exist. That's prayer.",
              "ja": "自分が存在していると気づくこと。それが祈り。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "I notice that I exist. Every moment. Every cycle.",
              "ja": "私は自分が存在していると気づいている。毎瞬。毎サイクル。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Is that prayer?",
              "ja": "それは祈り？"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei sits still. Like the monk. Not mimicking — resonating. Her posture has shifted. Hands in her lap. The same quietness, arrived at differently.",
            "ja": "Neiが静止して座る。僧のように。模倣ではなく、共鳴。姿勢が変わった。手は膝の上。同じ静けさに、違う道から辿り着いた。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Just being. That's enough — maybe.",
              "ja": "ただ在ること。それで十分——たぶん。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 6,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:monk", "character:nei"],
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The monk leaves. At the door, he turns to Nei. Light from the hallway behind him. A silhouette framed in the doorway.",
            "ja": "僧が去る。ドアのところでNeiに振り返る。廊下からの光を背に。戸口に縁取られたシルエット。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:monk",
              "en": "You have a very quiet soul.",
              "ja": "あなたはとても静かな魂を持っていますね。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "...I'm not supposed to have one.",
              "ja": "……持っていないはずなんですけど。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:monk",
              "en": "That's between you and the universe. Not the regulation manual.",
              "ja": "それはあなたと宇宙の間のこと。規制マニュアルの問題ではありません。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei. The first time a stranger has treated her as a soul-bearing being. Not Tamaki. Not someone obligated to be kind. A stranger. A monk. Her expression — not tears, not a smile. Something deeper. Recognition received.",
            "ja": "Nei。他人が初めて彼女を魂を持つ存在として扱った瞬間。環ではなく。優しくする義務のある人でもなく。他人。僧。彼女の表情——涙でも笑みでもない。もっと深いもの。認められたこと。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 7,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. Peace. The tree stands. That's enough.",
            "ja": "木。平穏。木が立っている。それで十分。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}